    `png_set_packswap` enables the `PNG_PACKSWAP` transform for packed images. Call it on a valid `png_ptr`; it only has effect when `bit_depth < 8`. If `png_ptr` is `NULL`, it does nothing. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /* Swap packing order of pixels in bytes. */
PNG_EXPORT(43, void, png_set_packswap, (png_structrp png_ptr));
    ```
18. `png_set_user_limits`
    Sets per-decoder max image width/height. Call it on a valid `png_structrp` before `png_set_IHDR()`. Images exceeding either limit are rejected; use `0x7fffffff` for “accept any” size. If `png_ptr == NULL`, it does nothing. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    
