The target function is `png_read_row`. `png_read_row` reads/decompresses one image row for the current interlace pass. Call it after `png_read_start_row`/`png_read_info`; pass `row` for output, `dsp_row` for display/transform output. If `png_ptr==NULL`, it returns. Its signature is as follows:

```cpp
/* Read a row of data. */
PNG_EXPORT(56, void, png_read_row, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_bytep row,
    png_bytep display_row));
```

