PNG_EXPORT(98, void, png_free_data, (png_const_structrp png_ptr,
    png_inforp info_ptr, png_uint_32 free_me, int num));
    ```
5. `png_write_sig`
    Writes the PNG 8-byte file signature to the output stream. Use it at the start of PNG writing; `sig_bytes` lets it write only the remaining bytes if some were already sent. If `sig_bytes < 3`, it marks the signature as present. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /* Write the PNG file signature. */
PNG_EXPORT(13, void, png_write_sig, (png_structrp png_ptr));
    ```
