    ```
10. `png_set_filter`
    `png_set_filter` selects libpng’s row-filtering for PNG writing. Use `method=0` (`PNG_FILTER_TYPE_BASE`) and a filter mask like `PNG_FILTER_VALUE_NONE/SUB/...`. Invalid filter bits can trigger an error; `png_ptr==NULL` is ignored. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    /* Set the filtering method(s) used by libpng.  Currently, the only valid
 * value for "method" is 0.
 */
PNG_EXPORT(67, void, png_set_filter, (png_structrp png_ptr, int method,
    int filters));
    ```
11. `png_set_packswap`
    `png_set_packswap` enables the `PNG_PACKSWAP` transform for packed images. Call it on a valid `png_ptr`; it only has effect when `bit_depth < 8`. If `png_ptr` is `NULL`, it does nothing. Its signature is:
