    ```
12. `png_set_user_limits`
    Sets per-decoder max image width/height. Call it on a valid `png_structrp` before `png_set_IHDR()`. Images exceeding either limit are rejected; use `0x7fffffff` for “accept any” size. If `png_ptr == NULL`, it does nothing. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    
PNG_EXPORT(186, void, png_set_user_limits, (png_structrp png_ptr,
    png_uint_32 user_width_max, png_uint_32 user_height_max));
    ```
13. `png_set_gAMA`
    `png_set_gAMA` sets the PNG gAMA chunk in `info_ptr` using a double gamma value. It just converts to libpng fixed-point via `png_set_gAMA_fixed`; actual validation/handling is in that helper. Use it when writing image gamma metadata. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    
PNG_FP_EXPORT(139, void, png_set_gAMA, (png_const_structrp png_ptr,
    png_inforp info_ptr, double file_gamma))
PNG_FIXED_EXPORT(140, void, png_set_gAMA_fixed, (png_const_structrp png_ptr,
    png_inforp info_ptr, png_fixed_point int_file_gamma))
#endif

#ifdef PNG_hIST_SUPPORTED
PNG_EXPORT(141, png_uint_32, png_get_hIST, (png_const_structrp png_ptr,
