    `png_read_png()` is a convenience “read whole image” API: it calls `png_read_info()`, applies requested transforms, then reads the image data. Use it only after setting up `png_ptr/info_ptr` and desired transform flags. If `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` is NULL it returns; oversized height triggers `png_error()`. Its signature is:
