    ```
8. `png_get_uint_31`
    `png_get_uint_31` reads a 32-bit big-endian value from `buf` and enforces PNG’s 31-bit unsigned limit. Use it when parsing fields that must fit in `0..PNG_UINT_31_MAX`. If the value is larger, it calls `png_error(png_ptr, "PNG unsigned integer out of range")`; otherwise it returns the value. Its signature is:
    ```cpp
    
