Task: Write a C++ fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libpng using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C++ source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

You should invoke the functions in the following order: `png_read_update_info` -> `png_malloc` -> `png_get_rowbytes` -> `png_read_row` -> `png_read_end` -> `png_destroy_read_struct`

Below is the detailed information:

1. `png_read_row`
​ `png_read_row` reads/decompresses one image row for the current interlace pass. Call it after `png_read_start_row`/`png_read_info`; pass `row` for output, `dsp_row` for display/transform output. If `png_ptr==NULL`, it returns.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Read a row of data. */
PNG_EXPORT(56, void, png_read_row, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_bytep row, png_bytep display_row));
​ ```

2. `png_destroy_read_struct`
​ Destroys a read-side PNG context and frees associated `png_info` structs. Call with pointers to `png_struct`, `info`, and optional `end_info`; any NULL arg is ignored. If `png_ptr` is NULL, it returns. On success, it NULLs `*png_ptr_ptr` and frees the read state.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Free any memory associated with the png_struct and the png_info_structs */
PNG_EXPORT(64, void, png_destroy_read_struct, (png_structpp png_ptr_ptr, png_infopp info_ptr_ptr, png_infopp end_info_ptr_ptr));
​ ```

3. `png_read_update_info`
​ Updates `info_ptr`/row state after setting read transforms, before reading rows. Call once after `png_read_info` and before `png_read_row`/`png_read_image`. If called twice, it reports a duplicate-call error; if `png_ptr` is NULL, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Optional call to update the users info structure */
PNG_EXPORT(54, void, png_read_update_info, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_inforp info_ptr));
​ ```

4. `png_malloc`
​ `png_malloc` allocates `size` bytes using libpng’s memory allocator tied to `png_ptr`. Use it only with a valid `png_ptr`; if `png_ptr==NULL` it returns `NULL`. On allocation failure it calls `png_error(png_ptr, "Out of memory")` instead of returning `NULL`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORTA(94, png_voidp, png_malloc, (png_const_structrp png_ptr, png_alloc_size_t size), PNG_ALLOCATED);
​ ```

5. `png_get_rowbytes`
​ `png_get_rowbytes` returns `info_ptr->rowbytes`: the byte count needed for one transformed image row. Call it with valid `png_ptr` and `info_ptr`; if either is `NULL`, it returns `0`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Returns number of bytes needed to hold a transformed row. */
PNG_EXPORT(111, size_t, png_get_rowbytes, (png_const_structrp png_ptr, png_const_inforp info_ptr));
​ ```

6. `png_read_end`
​ `png_read_end` finishes PNG input after image rows: it flushes any pending IDAT/zlib state, then reads remaining chunks to the end. Call it after `png_read_image`/row reads. If `png_ptr==NULL`, it returns; palette index issues may be reported as benign errors.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Read the end of the PNG file. */
PNG_EXPORT(62, void, png_read_end, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_inforp info_ptr));
​ ```

## Related Data Types

```cpp
struct png_info_def {
 /* The following are necessary for every PNG file */
 png_uint_32 width;
 /* valid chunk data (see PNG_INFO_ below) */
 size_t rowbytes;
 /* bytes needed to hold an untransformed row */
 png_colorp palette;
 /* array of color values (valid & PNG_INFO_PLTE) */
 png_uint_16 num_palette;
 /* number of transparent palette color (tRNS) */
 png_byte bit_depth;
 /* This is never set during write */
 png_byte signature[8];
 /* png_colorspace only contains 'flags' if neither GAMMA or COLORSPACE are
 * defined. When COLORSPACE is switched on all the colorspace-defining
 * chunks should be enabled, when GAMMA is switched on all the gamma-defining
 * chunks should be enabled. If this is not done it becomes possible to read
 * inconsistent PNG files and assign a probably incorrect interpretation to
 * the information. (In other words, by carefully choosing which chunks to
 * recognize the system configuration can select an interpretation for PNG
 * files containing ambiguous data and this will result in inconsistent
 * behavior between different libpng builds!)
 */
 png_colorspace colorspace;
 /* iCCP chunk data. */
 png_charp iccp_name;
 /* profile name */
 png_bytep iccp_profile;
 /* The tEXt, and zTXt chunks contain human-readable textual data in
 * uncompressed, compressed, and optionally compressed forms, respectively.
 * The data in "text" is an array of pointers to uncompressed,
 * null-terminated C strings. Each chunk has a keyword that describes the
 * textual data contained in that chunk. Keywords are not required to be
 * unique, and the text string may be empty. Any number of text chunks may
 * be in an image.
 */
 int num_text;
 /* current size of text array */
 png_textp text;
 /* The tIME chunk holds the last time the displayed image data was
 * modified. See the png_time struct for the contents of this struct.
 */
 png_time mod_time;
 /* The sBIT chunk specifies the number of significant high-order bits
 * in the pixel data. Values are in the range [1, bit_depth], and are
 * only specified for the channels in the pixel data. The contents of
 * the low-order bits is not specified. Data is valid if
 * (valid & PNG_INFO_sBIT) is non-zero.
 */
 png_color_8 sig_bit;
 /* alpha values for paletted image */
 png_color_16 trans_color;
 /* The oFFs chunk gives the offset in "offset_unit_type" units rightwards
 * and downwards from the top-left corner of the display, page, or other
 * application-specific co-ordinate space. See the PNG_OFFSET_ defines
 * below for the unit types. Valid if (valid & PNG_INFO_oFFs) non-zero.
 */
 png_int_32 x_offset;
 /* The hIST chunk contains the relative frequency or importance of the
 * various palette entries, so that a viewer can intelligently select a
 * reduced-color palette, if required. Data is an array of "num_palette"
 * values in the range [0,65535]. Data valid if (valid & PNG_INFO_hIST)
 * is non-zero.
 */
 png_uint_16p hist;
 /* Latin-1 string giving physical units */
 png_charpp pcal_params;
 /* Storage for unknown chunks that the library doesn't recognize. */
 png_unknown_chunkp unknown_chunks;
 /* Data on sPLT chunks (there may be more than one). */
 png_sPLT_tp splt_palettes;
 /* Memory has been allocated if (valid & PNG_ALLOCATED_INFO_ROWS)
 non-zero */
 /* Data valid if (valid & PNG_INFO_IDAT) non-zero */
 png_bytepp row_pointers;
 // ... methods are omitted
};

struct png_struct_def {
 jmp_buf jmp_buf_local;
 /* New name in 1.6.0 for jmp_buf in png_struct */
 png_longjmp_ptr longjmp_fn;
 /* setjmp non-local goto function. */
 jmp_buf *jmp_buf_ptr;
 /* passed to longjmp_fn */
 size_t jmp_buf_size;

 png_error_ptr error_fn;

 png_voidp error_ptr;
 /* user supplied struct for error functions */
 png_rw_ptr write_data_fn;

 png_user_transform_ptr read_user_transform_fn;
 /* user supplied struct for user transform */
 png_byte user_transform_depth;

 png_uint_32 mode;
 /* ID (chunk type) of zstream owner, 0 if none */
 z_stream zstream;

