​ `png_set_sig_bytes` tells libpng how many PNG signature bytes you already consumed before calling `png_read_info`. Use it after pre-reading 0–8 magic bytes. `num_bytes<0` is treated as 0; `>8` triggers `png_error`; `NULL` `png_ptr` is ignored.
