## Target API Functions

1. `png_malloc`
​ `png_malloc` allocates `size` bytes using libpng’s memory allocator tied to `png_ptr`. Use it only with a valid `png_ptr`; if `png_ptr==NULL` it returns `NULL`. On allocation failure it calls `png_error(png_ptr, "Out of memory")` instead of returning `NULL`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
