5. `png_malloc_default`
​ `png_malloc_default` is libpng’s built-in allocator: it ignores any app memory hook and uses `malloc` via `png_malloc_base(NULL, size)`. Use it only with a valid `png_ptr`. If `png_ptr==NULL`, it returns `NULL`; if allocation fails, it calls `png_error(png_ptr, "Out of Memory")`.
​ Its signature is:
