2. `png_get_mem_ptr`
​ `png_get_mem_ptr` returns the user-supplied `mem_ptr` stored in a `png_struct`. Use it to retrieve the pointer associated with custom memory alloc/free callbacks. If `png_ptr` is `NULL`, it returns `NULL`; otherwise it returns `png_ptr->mem_ptr`.
