 * smaller value of window_bits if it can do so safely.
 */
PNG_EXPORT(72, void, png_set_compression_window_bits, (png_structrp png_ptr, int window_bits));
​ ```

3. `png_set_text_compression_mem_level`
​ Sets the zlib memory level used when compressing text chunks. Call it with a valid `png_structrp` before writing text; `NULL` does nothing. It simply stores `mem_level` in `png_ptr->zlib_text_mem_level` with no validation.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORT(223, void, png_set_text_compression_mem_level, (png_structrp png_ptr, int mem_level));
​ ```

4. `png_set_text_compression_level`
​ Sets the zlib compression level for non-IDAT text chunks. Call it with a valid `png_ptr` before writing text; if `png_ptr` is `NULL`, it returns. It only stores `level` in `png_ptr->zlib_text_level`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
