​ ```

4. `png_save_uint_32`
​ `png_save_uint_32` stores a 32-bit `png_uint_32` into a 4-byte buffer in big-endian/network order. Use it when writing PNG data fields to a byte array. It always writes 4 bytes; `buf` must be valid for 4 bytes.
