​ ```

6. `png_get_uint_32`
​ `png_get_uint_32` converts 4 bytes in `buf` from PNG/network byte order (big-endian) into a `png_uint_32`. Use it when reading 32-bit values from PNG data. It just combines the 4 bytes; no validation or bounds checking.
