​ ```

2. `png_set_sRGB`
​ `png_set_sRGB` marks the image as sRGB and records the rendering intent. Call it only with valid `png_ptr` and `info_ptr`; if either is `NULL`, it returns immediately. It updates `info_ptr->colorspace` via `png_colorspace_set_sRGB` and syncs the info struct.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORT(156, void, png_set_sRGB, (png_const_structrp png_ptr, png_inforp info_ptr, int srgb_intent));
​ ```

3. `png_write_info_before_PLTE`
​ Writes the PNG signature and IHDR before PLTE. Call it once with valid `png_ptr`/`info_ptr`; if either is NULL it returns. Repeated calls are ignored via `PNG_WROTE_INFO_BEFORE_PLTE`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Writes all the PNG information before the image. */
PNG_EXPORT(20, void, png_write_info_before_PLTE,
 (png_structrp png_ptr, png_const_inforp info_ptr));
​ ```

4. `png_write_end`
​ `png_write_end` finishes PNG writing. Call it after all IDAT/image data are written; `info_ptr` may supply trailing chunks (e.g. tIME/text). If no IDATs were written, it errors. If `png_ptr` is NULL, it returns.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
