PNG_EXPORT(20, void, png_write_info_before_PLTE,
 (png_structrp png_ptr, png_const_inforp info_ptr));
​ ```

4. `png_write_end`
​ `png_write_end` finishes PNG writing. Call it after all IDAT/image data are written; `info_ptr` may supply trailing chunks (e.g. tIME/text). If no IDATs were written, it errors. If `png_ptr` is NULL, it returns.
​ Its signature is:
