Task: Write a C++ fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libpng using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C++ source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `png_set_gray_to_rgb`
​ `png_set_gray_to_rgb` enables a read transform that expands grayscale images to RGB. Use it before reading rows. It also forces 1/2/4-bit gray to 8-bit first. If read transforms aren’t allowed, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Expand the grayscale to 24-bit RGB if necessary. */
PNG_EXPORT(31, void, png_set_gray_to_rgb, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

2. `png_write_sig`
​ Writes the PNG 8-byte file signature to the output stream. Use it at the start of PNG writing; `sig_bytes` lets it write only the remaining bytes if some were already sent. If `sig_bytes < 3`, it marks the signature as present.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Write the PNG file signature. */
PNG_EXPORT(13, void, png_write_sig, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

3. `png_set_packing`
​ `png_set_packing` requests unpacking 1/2/4-bit samples to 1 byte each. Call it on a valid `png_ptr` before read/write processing. If `bit_depth < 8`, it sets `PNG_PACK` (and write `usr_bit_depth=8`); otherwise it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Use 1 byte per pixel in 1, 2, or 4-bit depth files. */
PNG_EXPORT(42, void, png_set_packing, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

4. `png_set_packswap`
​ `png_set_packswap` enables the `PNG_PACKSWAP` transform for packed images. Call it on a valid `png_ptr`; it only has effect when `bit_depth < 8`. If `png_ptr` is `NULL`, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Swap packing order of pixels in bytes. */
PNG_EXPORT(43, void, png_set_packswap, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

5. `png_write_row`
​ `png_write_row` writes one image row to a PNG stream. Call it after `png_write_info`; on the first row it checks setup/transforms. If `png_ptr` is NULL it returns. Missing `png_write_info` triggers `png_error`; unsupported set transforms may warn.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Write a row of image data */
PNG_EXPORT(58, void, png_write_row, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_const_bytep row));
​ ```

6. `png_write_png`
​ `png_write_png` is a high-level write helper: it writes PNG header/info, applies requested write transforms, then writes image data. Use it only with valid `png_ptr`/`info_ptr` and existing rows (`PNG_INFO_IDAT`); otherwise it returns or errors. Unsupported transforms trigger an app error.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORT(179, void, png_write_png, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_inforp info_ptr, int transforms, png_voidp params));
​ ```

