Task: Write a C++ fuzz driver program to fuzz the library libpng using the information provided below. Reply with only the content of the C++ source file enclosed in triple backticks (```), without any additional explanation.

## Target API Functions

1. `png_set_keep_unknown_chunks`
​ Sets libpng’s policy for unknown chunks: `keep` chooses default handling; `chunk_list`/`num_chunks` can override per-chunk. `num_chunks<=0` only sets the default. `png_ptr==NULL` returns; invalid `keep` triggers app error.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORT(172, void, png_set_keep_unknown_chunks, (png_structrp png_ptr, int keep, png_const_bytep chunk_list, int num_chunks));
​ ```

2. `png_get_chunk_cache_max`
​ Returns the user-set maximum number of unknown chunks libpng will cache. Use it with a valid `png_ptr`; if `png_ptr` is `NULL`, it returns `0`. It only reports `png_ptr->user_chunk_cache_max`, no other behavior.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORT(190, png_uint_32, png_get_chunk_cache_max,
 (png_const_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

3. `png_set_chunk_cache_max`
​ `png_set_chunk_cache_max` sets `png_ptr->user_chunk_cache_max`, i.e. the maximum number of chunks libpng will cache. Call it on a valid `png_structrp` before reading. If `png_ptr` is `NULL`, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Added in libpng-1.4.0 */
PNG_EXPORT(189, void, png_set_chunk_cache_max, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_uint_32 user_chunk_cache_max));
​ ```

4. `png_set_chunk_malloc_max`
​ Sets `png_ptr->user_chunk_malloc_max`, i.e. the max malloc size allowed for a chunk. Call it on a valid `png_structrp`; if `png_ptr` is NULL, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Added in libpng-1.4.1 */
PNG_EXPORT(191, void, png_set_chunk_malloc_max, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_alloc_size_t user_chunk_cache_max));
​ ```

5. `png_read_end`
​ `png_read_end` finishes PNG input after image rows: it flushes any pending IDAT/zlib state, then reads remaining chunks to the end. Call it after `png_read_image`/row reads. If `png_ptr==NULL`, it returns; palette index issues may be reported as benign errors.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Read the end of the PNG file. */
PNG_EXPORT(62, void, png_read_end, (png_structrp png_ptr, png_inforp info_ptr));
​ ```

6. `png_get_chunk_malloc_max`
​ `png_get_chunk_malloc_max()` is a simple getter for the current per-chunk allocation limit. Call it with a valid `png_ptr`; it returns `png_ptr->user_chunk_malloc_max`. If `png_ptr` is `NULL`, it returns `0`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORT(192, png_alloc_size_t, png_get_chunk_malloc_max,
 (png_const_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

