3. `png_set_scale_16`
​ `png_set_scale_16` requests libpng to accurately scale 16-bit samples down to 8-bit during read. Call it on a valid `png_ptr` before reading rows. If read transforms aren’t allowed (`png_rtran_ok` fails), it does nothing; otherwise it sets `PNG_SCALE_16_TO_8`.
​ Its signature is:
