​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Use blue, green, red order for pixels. */
PNG_EXPORT(30, void, png_set_bgr, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

2. `png_set_expand`
​ `png_set_expand` enables automatic expansion transforms. Use it before reading rows to request palette/low-bit/packed/gray+tRNS data be expanded to 8-bit grayscale or 24-bit RGB, with alpha when available. If transforms aren’t allowed, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Expand data to 24-bit RGB, or 8-bit grayscale, with alpha if available. */
PNG_EXPORT(26, void, png_set_expand, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

3. `png_start_read_image`
​ Starts row/image read setup. Call once before reading image data, typically after `png_read_update_info`. If row init hasn’t run, it calls `png_read_start_row`; if called twice, it reports a duplicate-call app error.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Optional update palette with requested transformations */
PNG_EXPORT(53, void, png_start_read_image, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

4. `png_set_expand_gray_1_2_4_to_8`
​ Enables expansion of low-bit-depth grayscale (1/2/4-bit) to 8-bit during read. Call it on a valid `png_structrp` before row reading; it just sets `PNG_EXPAND` if transforms are allowed, otherwise it returns with no effect.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORT(27, void, png_set_expand_gray_1_2_4_to_8, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

5. `png_set_expand_16`
​ `png_set_expand_16()` enables read-side expansion to 16-bit channels. Use it before `png_read_info()`/row reads. It sets `PNG_EXPAND_16|PNG_EXPAND|PNG_EXPAND_tRNS`, so palette data becomes RGB and any tRNS chunk is expanded; if transforms aren’t allowed, it does nothing.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
/* Expand to 16-bit channels, forces conversion of palette to RGB and expansion
 * of a tRNS chunk if present.
 */
PNG_EXPORT(221, void, png_set_expand_16, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

6. `png_set_palette_to_rgb`
​ `png_set_palette_to_rgb` requests libpng to expand paletted images to full RGB, and also expand tRNS transparency if present. Call it before reading image rows. If transformations are already locked out, it does nothing; otherwise it sets `PNG_EXPAND | PNG_EXPAND_tRNS`.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
PNG_EXPORT(28, void, png_set_palette_to_rgb, (png_structrp png_ptr));
​ ```

