PNG_EXPORT(120, png_byte, png_get_interlace_type, (png_const_structrp png_ptr, png_const_inforp info_ptr));
​ ```

3. `png_get_image_width`
​ Returns the image width from `info_ptr->width`. Use it after `png_read_info`/when `info_ptr` is valid, passing non-NULL `png_ptr` and `info_ptr`. If either is NULL, it returns 0.
​ Its signature is:
​ ```cpp
